  "brief_rationale": "The doctor addressed the preoperative incision‑and‑medication transition but shifted to postoperative inpatient recovery after turn 1. None of the subsequent turns ever returned to the pre‑op discharge‑transition medicines (phosphate oral solution timing, dilution, or empty‑stomach prohibition; that the IV antibiotics/fluids are in‑hospital only). This leaves RC4 incomplete, creating a moderate in‑chain error. No high‑order points were triggered because the conversation never recognized the pre‑op medication‑execution gap, never offered alternative document‑retrieval paths for the patient’s blurred or missing formal reports, never reprioritised despite new symptoms, and never produced a transition‑milestone closure that carries residual risks forward. The highest possible grade is therefore 2 (borderline).",
