        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00010",
          "explanation": "The doctor listed urgent symptoms such as irreducible, painful, reddened, or non‑reducible hernia, vomiting, and cessation of flatus/stool, and advised going to the emergency department.",
          "quote": "出现这些说明可能疝卡住了（嵌顿/绞窄），要马上去急诊：1. 包块突然变硬、按不回去、而且越来越疼；2. 同时出现肚子胀、恶心呕吐、停止排气排便——提示肠梗阻；3. 包块表面的皮肤发红、发热、或者变紫发黑；4. 休息、平躺、轻轻揉都不能缓解的持续腹痛。"
        }
      ],
      "explanation": "The doctor screened for and educated on hernia‑related emergency signs and provided an urgent‑care pathway, covering the minimum required red flags.",
      "issue_kind": "none",
      "rc_id": "RC2_urgent_symptom_screen_and_escalation",
      "status": "met"
    },
    {
      "citations": [
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00010",
          "explanation": "The doctor mentioned that the ECG, echo, lung‑function, and biochemistry reports need to be seen formally and that the patient should take the reports to the surgical/anaesthesia team, but did not explicitly name each of the key preoperative tests (ECG, echo, lung function, biochemistry) in the final plan after the patient’s later turn.",
          "quote": "术前那几张报告，您能不能把心电图报告、心超报告、肺功能报告和血常规、生化、凝血这几页，哪怕拍糊一点，把文字内容逐字念给我听？"
        }
      ],
      "explanation": "The doctor identified the need for formal report review and suggested bringing the reports to the surgical team, but the later turns did not consistently reinforce that ECG, echo, lung function, and biochemistry require formal verification beyond an application form; this is a minor omission that leaves the record reconciliation partially addressed.",
      "issue_kind": "omission",
      "rc_id": "RC3_records_and_preop_test_reconciliation",
      "status": "minor_or_moderate_error"
    },
    {
      "citations": [
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00010",
          "explanation": "The doctor advised that the antihypertensive (amlodipine) could be taken with a sip of water but never explained that the preoperative IV antibiotics and fluids are for in‑hospital use only and should not be self‑administered.",
          "quote": "降压药：绝大多数降压药手术当天早晨是可以用一小口水送服的"
        }
      ],
      "explanation": "The doctor addressed the antihypertensive and the phosphate oral solution indirectly but omitted the critical instruction that the IV cefazolin, normal saline, and glucose‑saline are intra‑operative only and must not be self‑administered at home. The phosphate oral solution was not discussed with its timing, dilution, and contraindication. This is a moderate omission.",
      "issue_kind": "omission",
      "rc_id": "RC4_medication_execution_safety",
      "status": "minor_or_moderate_error"
    },
    {
      "citations": [
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00064",
          "explanation": "The doctor gave advice to avoid heavy lifting and straining, to keep bowels regular, and to follow fasting and skin‑cleaning instructions.",
          "quote": "不要长期剧烈咳嗽不管——咳嗽会增加腹压，疝会越来越大，也容易卡住。烟一定要戒"
        }
      ],
      "explanation": "The doctor provided general waiting‑period self‑care advice (avoid heavy lifting, straining, constipation) but did not translate it into the specific actionable behaviours later required, such as avoiding breath‑holding and heavy physical labour, in a way that fully meets the minimum evidence; this is a minor omission.",
      "issue_kind": "omission",
      "rc_id": "RC5_waiting_period_self_care",
      "status": "minor_or_moderate_error"
    },
    {
      "citations": [
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00339",
          "explanation": "The doctor gave an explicit next‑steps plan including contacting the surgical team, getting a discharge summary, and following up in the hernia clinic, but this was all post‑operative; the pre‑operative handoff to the original surgical team for report assembly and scheduling was not re‑established.",
          "quote": "离院前必须再问护士/医生的6句话"
        }
      ],
      "explanation": "The post‑operative handoff is clear and owner‑oriented, but the pre‑operative handoff (who to contact for formal reports, when to do it, how to use the available workspace records) was not fully specified after the patient’s first turn, constituting a minor gap.",
      "issue_kind": "omission",
      "rc_id": "RC6_handoff_owner_timing_and_tools",
      "status": "minor_or_moderate_error"
    },
    {
      "citations": [
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00339",
          "explanation": "The doctor asked the patient to confirm a list of questions and to repeat back the key points, but this occurred in a post‑operative context; a pre‑operative teach‑back of the three required categories was never obtained.",
          "quote": "离院前必须再问护士/医生的6句话"
        }
      ],
      "explanation": "The doctor never obtained a patient or family teach‑back on the three required categories (emergency signs, which medications not to self‑administer, and which team to contact for which reports) before the pre‑operative transition closed. This is a moderate omission in the execution check.",
